# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Zola build output
site/public/

# Internal-only documents (not published) — the architecture notes, the backlog,
# and under `references/` the third-party specifications and reference
# implementations they are written against. `D` and `R` numbers are resolvable
# only inside this folder, so nothing in the published tree may cite one; see
# concepts/README.md.
#
# The references are copyrighted publications and are not redistributed here.
# `concepts/references/README.md` records every retrieval URL and
# `concepts/references/fetch.sh` rebuilds the folder from scratch, so an index
# entry with no file is fine and a file with no entry is invisible.
concepts/

# Agent instructions — the round procedure and whatever else is added beside it.
# Internal for the same reason `concepts/` is: it cites `D` and `R` numbers, names
# specific past defects, and describes the private design folder it operates on,
# none of which resolves for a reader of the published tree.
.claude/

# Feature specifications and the Spec Kit machinery that produces them: one
# `specs/NNN-slug/` per roadmap item, the constitution plans are checked against,
# and the `/speckit-*` skills under `.claude/`. Internal for the same reason as
# `concepts/` — they cite its numbers — so nothing published may cite a path in
# either.
/specs/
/.specify/

# Custom
.DS_Store

# Build output for the container image (see `just image`).
dist/
